# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
# Scratch build trees, as a GLOB rather than one pattern per ticket (KAN-516).
#
# This block used to enumerate them — `dist-unfixed/` for the baseline
# verify-mcp-runtime-validation.mjs compares against, `dist-guardless-*/` for
# the copy verify-board-reconciler-guard.mjs tears the fleet down with,
# `dist-kan342-red-*/` for verify-absence-is-not-intent.mjs's red drive. Each
# was added AFTER a `git add -A` had already swept that tree into a commit,
# KAN-368's note recording 58 files on the third occasion.
#
# An enumeration requires every future red drive to remember to extend it, and
# fails silently and hugely when one does not: KAN-516 committed 81,309 lines
# across two `dist-kan343-*` trees, and every required check passed on them.
# `dist-kan342-red-*` was listed; `dist-kan343-*` was not, because nobody had
# got to it yet. The glob needs nobody to remember.
#
# Checked safe rather than assumed: `git ls-tree -r origin/main` matched no
# tracked path against `(^|/)dist-`, so this newly ignores nothing.
dist-*/

# Logs
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
